- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/legal-body/ukpga/2002/16/section/4
  '@type': schema:CreativeWork
  route: legal-body/ukpga/2002/16/section/4
  title: 'ukpga/2002/16/section/4 — State pension credit: entitlement and amount / Exclusions'
  type: Statutory body evidence
  status: draft
  authority: Machine extraction from official legislation publication; unreviewed
  review_status: unreviewed
  resource: https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2002/16/section/4/2026-09-20
  license: https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
  description: 'Requested source version 2026-09-20. Observed extent attributes: E+W+S. Complete selected
    unit with whitespace-normalised numbered blocks; editorial commentary and amendment structure remain
    in the linked projection. Legal applicability, commencement, complete effects and specialist review
    remain unestablished.'
  body: "4\n1\nA claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other
    member of which is entitled to state pension credit.\n1A\nA claimant is not entitled to state pension
    credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which has not attained the qualifying age.\n\
    2\nIn section 115(1) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 (c. 33) (exclusion of certain persons
    from benefits) in the words preceding paragraph (a), after “Jobseekers Act 1995” insert “ or to state
    pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002 ”.\n3\nWhere the amount payable by way of state
    pension credit would (apart from this subsection) be less than a prescribed amount, it shall not be
    payable except in prescribed circumstances."
  context_assembly:
    kind: evidence
    text: "4\n1\nA claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the
      other member of which is entitled to state pension credit.\n1A\nA claimant is not entitled to state
      pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which has not attained the qualifying
      age.\n2\nIn section 115(1) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 (c. 33) (exclusion of certain
      persons from benefits) in the words preceding paragraph (a), after “Jobseekers Act 1995” insert
      “ or to state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002 ”.\n3\nWhere the amount payable
      by way of state pension credit would (apart from this subsection) be less than a prescribed amount,
      it shall not be payable except in prescribed circumstances."
