- '@id':
    https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/legal-body/uksi/2002/1792/schedule/II/paragraph/3
  '@type': schema:CreativeWork
  route: legal-body/uksi/2002/1792/schedule/II/paragraph/3
  title: uksi/2002/1792/schedule/II/paragraph/3 — Circumstances in which a person is liable to meet
    housing costs
  type: Statutory body evidence
  status: draft
  authority: Machine extraction from official legislation publication; unreviewed
  review_status: unreviewed
  resource: https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2002/1792/schedule/II/paragraph/3/2026-09-20
  license: https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
  description: 'Requested source version 2026-09-20. Observed extent attributes: unknown. Complete selected
    unit with whitespace-normalised numbered blocks; editorial commentary and amendment structure remain
    in the linked projection. Legal applicability, commencement, complete effects and specialist review
    remain unestablished.'
  body: "3\nA person is liable to meet housing costs where—\na\nthe liability falls upon him or his partner
    but not where the liability is to a member of the same household as the person on whom the liability
    falls;\nb\nbecause the person liable to meet the housing costs is not meeting them, the claimant has
    to meet those costs in order to continue to live in the dwelling occupied as the home and it is reasonable
    in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to meet those costs;\nc\nhe in practice shares
    the housing costs with other members of the household none of whom are close relatives either of the
    claimant or his partner, and\ni\none or more of those members is liable to meet those costs, and\n\
    ii\nit is reasonable in the circumstances to treat him as sharing responsibility."
  context_assembly:
    kind: evidence
    text: "3\nA person is liable to meet housing costs where—\na\nthe liability falls upon him or his
      partner but not where the liability is to a member of the same household as the person on whom the
      liability falls;\nb\nbecause the person liable to meet the housing costs is not meeting them, the
      claimant has to meet those costs in order to continue to live in the dwelling occupied as the home
      and it is reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to meet those costs;\n\
      c\nhe in practice shares the housing costs with other members of the household none of whom are
      close relatives either of the claimant or his partner, and\ni\none or more of those members is liable
      to meet those costs, and\nii\nit is reasonable in the circumstances to treat him as sharing responsibility."
